LightningSim is used as a runtime dependency. The local modified Python/Rust
backend, C++ trace-runtime source, frontend, and upstream build recipe are
included in third_party/lightningsim. LightningSim was developed by Rishov
Sarkar and Sharc Lab, Georgia Institute of Technology:
https://github.com/sharc-lab/LightningSim

These third-party sources retain their GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 only (AGPL-3.0-only), in third_party/lightningsim/LICENSE. The SGRM
Apache license does not replace that license. Local adaptations and
source-release packaging adjustments are documented in
third_party/lightningsim/LOCAL_CHANGES.md. The unmodified LLVM instrumenter,
SystemC runtime, and prebuilt web assets are provided by the pinned upstream
Conda package, not by private binaries committed to this repository.

The optional Stream-HLS benchmark source bundle contains code and workload
inputs from https://github.com/UCLA-VAST/Stream-HLS. The upstream MIT license
is preserved as STREAM_HLS_LICENSE inside that bundle. These third-party
benchmark files remain subject to that license; the SGRM license does not
replace it. AMD tool binaries and vendor headers are not redistributed.
